From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:21:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: emulate texture border colors on Xenos

Xenos has two border colors, (0, 0, 0, 0) and (1, 1, 1, 1) (fetch
constant dword 5 bits 0-1), and with point sampling it never reads the
border: CLAMP_TO_BORDER and MIRROR_CLAMP_TO_BORDER clamp to the edge.
Linear filtering does read it.

- Pick the white border when the border color is white.
- Fragment shader variants keyed per sampler (ir2_shader_variant.border),
  the color in IR2_BORDER_CONST + sampler with the view's swizzle:
  - nearest: select the color where a coordinate on a border axis is
    outside [0, 1] (|x| > 1 mirrored once);
  - linear, any other color: fetch again from a copy of the fetch
    constant with the white border, in a vertex texture slot left free
    (31 - k, up to six, with no more than 8 vertex samplers); per channel
    black + (white - black) * color, exact for any filter and level.
- 1D textures are sampled as 2D one texel high: force wrap_t to repeat,
  GL_CLAMP blended the border in along t.

piglit: 29 border tests pass (texwrap *bordercolor*, tex3d-depth1,
tex-border-1, gl-1.4-tex1d-2dborder). Not covered: rectangle textures,
16F/32F formats, more than six linear samplers. dEQP 17063/17075, no
regressions; performance unchanged.

